---
import MarketingLayout from "../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../lib/site";
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="About Boopity"
  description="Why Boopity is open source, who makes it, and what it means to run it for your pet-care business."
>
  <article class="wrap py-14 sm:py-20">
    <header class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-5 text-forest">About Boopity</p>
      <h1 class="display text-balance text-5xl sm:text-6xl">
        Built for independent pet sitters.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-7 max-w-2xl text-xl leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Boopity brings bookings, pet-care details, and payments together on your
        own website. It’s an open-source project by {site.owner}.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section
      class="mt-12 grid items-start gap-10 border-t border-line pt-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.15fr_.85fr] lg:gap-16"
      aria-labelledby="why-open-source"
    >
      <div>
        <h2 id="why-open-source" class="display text-3xl sm:text-4xl">
          Why we opened the code.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed">
          Boopity began as a subscription app. We chose to make it open source
          so sitters could install it for their own businesses, on a host they
          choose.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          You use your business name, logo, and colors. You decide which
          services clients can book and when. The source code is available under
          the MIT license, so you can use it, change it, and share your
          improvements.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link mt-5 inline-block" href={site.appRepository}>
          Explore the code on GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
      <aside
        class="rounded-2xl bg-sand p-7 sm:p-8"
        aria-labelledby="your-installation"
      >
        <h3 id="your-installation" class="text-xl font-semibold">
          Free software. Your own installation.
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
          Boopity doesn’t charge a software subscription or take a cut of
          bookings. Hosting, email, and payment-processing fees are separate.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
          You or your installer handles hosting, updates, and backups. The
          guides walk you through getting started.
        </p>
        <a
          class="text-link mt-5 inline-block"
          href="/docs/getting-started/installation/"
        >
          See what’s involved
        </a>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-10 border-t border-line pt-10 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-16">
      <section aria-labelledby="contribute">
        <h2 id="contribute" class="display text-3xl">
          Help shape Boopity.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Found a confusing step or something that doesn’t work? Tell us on
          GitHub. Bug reports, clearer instructions, and code contributions all
          help—you don’t have to be a developer to contribute.
        </p>
        <a
          class="text-link mt-5 inline-block"
          href={`${site.appRepository}/issues`}
        >
          Share feedback or report a bug
        </a>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="support">
        <h2 id="support" class="display text-3xl">
          Need a hand?
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Start with the{" "}
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/help/troubleshooting/">
            troubleshooting guide
          </a>
          , or ask a question on GitHub. Help is community-led, with no
          guaranteed response time.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Keep client details and credentials out of public posts. Report
          security concerns privately using the{" "}
          <a class="text-link" href={`${site.appRepository}/security/policy`}>
            security policy
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</MarketingLayout>
